  "mn74:14.1": "Following the Thai edition of the Canon. The Burmese and PTS editions say that Ven. Sāriputta was standing.",
  "mn74:14.2": "",
  "mn74:14.3": "The Pali word <i>no</i> in this sentence can mean either “indeed” or “to us.” Compare this account of Ven. Sāriputta’s awakening with the account given in <a href='https://suttacentral.net/mn111'>MN 111</a>.",
  "mn74:14.4": "",
  "mn74:15.1": "",
  "mn74:15.2": "",
  "mn74:15.3": "",
  "mn74:16.1": "",
  "mn74:16.2": "",
  "mn74:16.3": "",
  "mn74:16.4": "The Commentary states that after delivering this discourse the Buddha returned to the Bamboo Forest outside of Rājagaha and met with 1,250 arahant disciples to deliver the Ovāda Pāṭimokkha—the event commemorated every year on Māgha Pūjā.",
  "mn74:16.5": ""
